Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 20:52:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10960/11362] Emit the generator's induce-channel counters on
 every eval row

The proposer counts what the generator actually returned -- chat_completions,
chars_final, chars_reasoning -- and the only code that read them into an
artifact was arc_scored_path_lever_harness.py, frozen on the retired
Qwen3.5-9B-MTP pin and unable to start against the live generator.

So all eleven artifacts in results/arc_leaderboard_eval_runs/ carry zero rows
with these counters, including runs whose own llm_reached is true. The practical
cost surfaced today: after the n_ctx=98304 fix, "did the induce tier emit
anything" is not answerable from any artifact, and I was about to spend hours on
a live run that would have produced another row that could not answer it.

Same shape as REQ-ARC-WMTE-6640 three days ago: a diagnostic that exists on the
object, has one caller, and that caller cannot run. Fixed the same way and
deliberately placed beside it, so the two read as one rule rather than two
accidents.

An absent proposer is reported as a STATE rather than an error, because the LLM
tier legitimately may never fire and conflating those is the ambiguity the
sibling requirement exists to prevent. A missing or non-dict channel_totals is
an error marker, because an absent field reads as zero to a flat consumer.

Six tests. Two mutations, both RED: dropping the row wiring while leaving the
helper intact -- the incident's exact shape, a helper nothing calls -- and
turning the absent-proposer state into an error. Byte-identical restores, GREEN.

